    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"During the period July 5 through July 10, 1981, two (2) Vertical Seismic Profiles (VSPís) were recorded in the Edward J. Kubat, Government #1 Well, located approximately 18 miles west of \r\nBlanding, Utah, in San Juan County (Sec 23, T. 37 S., R. 19 E.).  The data were recorded by Grant Geophysical Corporation, under contract to the U.S. Geological Survey.  This CD-ROM publication contains the entire, unprocessed, data set contained in two (2) SEG-Y format files, and support information, sufficient to allow the user to process the data set.  The support information is contained in this file (A_README.1ST), the trace headers of each SEG-Y file, and one text file associated with each SEG-Y file. Furthermore, there are six (6) figures, referenced in the text of this document, contained in separate files in bitmap format which \r\nillustrate the location of the survey, geometrical configuration of the source and receivers, and partially processed parts of the data set.  An IBM P/C compatible seismic display program and trace-dump program are included on this disc for the purpose of \r\ndisplaying and examining the SEG-Y data files.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
    ],
